# Tokens and secrets for the devcontainer. Read by fish
# (.devcontainer/fish/config.fish) at every new shell start — never by Docker
# Compose, so the values stay out of the devcontainer start log and
# `docker inspect`. Never add .env.credentials to `env_file` in
# docker-compose.yml, or every token lands in the start log.
#
# Not a secret from the agent: Claude runs in a shell with these variables
# exported and can read every value. Use tokens with the narrowest scope that
# works.
#
# This .example file is never read — it documents the format. Copy the keys
# you need into .devcontainer/.env.credentials (gitignored) and fill them in.
#
# Adding or changing a key takes effect in the next new shell, no rebuild
# needed. Removing a key does not: the reader only sets keys it finds, and
# new VS Code terminals inherit the environment cached at container start —
# a removed key stays set until the container restarts. Revoke a leaked
# token at the provider; removing it here is not enough.
#
# Format: KEY=value lines. The value is everything after the first `=`,
# taken literally — no quote stripping, no $ or (...) expansion. Lines
# starting with # and blank lines are skipped.
#
# Recommended: chmod 600 .devcontainer/.env.credentials

# GITHUB_TOKEN=
